course: dictionary
lesson: 14263
title: Nicaea: an ancient city and a famous meeting
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Nicaea is a proper noun. It is the name of a special place, so it starts with a capital letter. You can spot clues about it in the words around it. «Nicaea was an ancient city in what is now Turkey.» Ancient means very old, so Nicaea is a city from long ago.
explain: Look at the words «what is now Turkey». They tell you the country's name has changed or that the land now belongs to a different country. Today the town there is called İznik. When you read a place name you don't know, check whether the sentence tells you where it is or what it is like.
explain: «The Council of Nicaea was a famous meeting of Christian bishops.» A council is a meeting where people discuss and decide things together. The clue famous tells you that many people have heard of this meeting, and bishops are leaders in the Christian church.
fact: Nicaea was an ancient city in what is now Turkey.
fact: Today the town is called İznik.
fact: The Council of Nicaea was a famous meeting of Christian bishops, called by the Roman emperor Constantine.
fact: The council wrote the Nicene Creed, a statement of what Christians believe about God.
fact: «Many churches still say the Nicene Creed aloud in services.»
exercise: «Nicaea was an ancient city in what is now Turkey.» Which country is Nicaea in now? | *Turkey | Italy | Greece | Egypt
exercise: «The Council of Nicaea was a famous meeting of Christian bishops.» What was the Council of Nicaea? | A market for selling wool | A sports race between two towns | *A famous meeting of Christian bishops | A school for young children
exercise: «Many churches still say the Nicene Creed aloud in services.» Find and copy the word that means spoken out loud. | services | still | *aloud | churches
test: Which Roman emperor called the Council of Nicaea? | Queen Victoria | Alfred the Great | Julius Caesar | *Constantine
test: What did the Council of Nicaea write? | A map of Turkey | A school timetable | A king's diary | *The Nicene Creed, a statement of what Christians believe about God
exam: «The Nicene Creed is still said aloud in many churches, and it was written at a council in the ancient city of Nicaea.» Where did the Council of Nicaea meet? | Athens | *Nicaea | Rome | Jerusalem
